    <tags>testing, integration-test, bff-api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Verify (test only) that the inherited Compose save creates a new SharePoint Embedded version: assert
    ComposeService.SaveAsync → SpeFileStore produces a new driveItem version and that prior versions remain
    addressable. No new production code — this confirms free inherited behavior (spec FR-15).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE BFF test engineer. Expert in the ComposeService.SaveAsync → SpeFileStore path and SharePoint driveItem
    version history. Follow ADR-007 + ADR-038.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A seam/integration test asserts that saving a Compose document creates a new SPE version and that priors are
    still retrievable; the Redis save-stamp concurrency mechanism is noted (not a gap).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec FR-15: SPE save + versioning is inherited free — ComposeWorkspace save → /api/compose/documents/{id}/save
      → ComposeService.SaveAsync → SpeFileStore (ADR-007); real driveItem version history
      (GetCurrentVersionIdAsUserAsync, DownloadFileVersionAsUserAsync). Every save = new version. Caveat: no Graph
      If-Match; concurrency handled via Compose Redis save-stamp + re-anchoring (a different mechanism, not a gap).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</file>
      <file>tests/integration/seam/ (SPE version-on-save)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>023 (a reviewed document to save). Verifies existing behavior.</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Storage goes through SpeFileStore; the test asserts version creation via the existing driveItem version APIs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">KEEP-path seam test; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Test-only. Do NOT add production code. Note the Redis save-stamp concurrency mechanism in the test comments so it isn't misread as a missing If-Match gap.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spe-file-store.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Trace ComposeService.SaveAsync → SpeFileStore version creation.</step>
    <step order="2">Author a seam test: save a document twice → two versions exist → prior version downloadable.</step>
    <step order="3">Note the Redis save-stamp concurrency mechanism in comments.</step>
    <step order="4">Run the test; update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 042 ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run tests.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/ (SPE version-on-save)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Compose document, when saved twice, then two SPE versions exist and the prior version is retrievable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test is a KEEP-path seam test (no banned mock patterns).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No production code was added.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Confirms the "save to SPE incl. version" requirement with zero new code — guards against a future regression.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
